# Line-ending policy, deliberately narrow: adding a rule here renormalizes
# exactly the files it names instead of the whole tree.
#
# `install.ps1` targets Windows and is committed with CRLF; it is intentionally
# NOT declared here. Adding a `text eol=crlf` rule would normalize the stored
# blob to LF and rewrite every line of the file in the index for no behavioral
# gain. (The former `*.sh text eol=lf` rule belonged to the removed Unix
# `install.sh`; no shell scripts remain in the tree.)
